<h1>The Homepage</h1>

<p>
    The homepage is your daily command center. It's the first thing you see when you log in, and it's designed to give you a complete picture of what needs your attention today.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Full-page screenshot of the homepage showing all three columns (left, middle, right) with all widgets visible. Use labels or callouts to identify the main sections: Daily Task List, Renewal Flow Tasks, Work tiles, and Alerts. -->

<h2>Understanding the Layout</h2>

<p>
    The homepage is organized into three columns:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Left column</strong> – Your personal task management (Daily Task List and Renewal Flow Tasks)</li>
    <li><strong>Middle column</strong> - High-volume work items that need quick action (Proposals, Certificates, Leads, etc.)</li>
    <li><strong>Right column</strong> – Alerts and reminders (Expiring Soon, Incomplete Tasks)</li>
</ul>

<p>
    This layout helps you prioritize: personal tasks on the left, urgent work in the middle, and important alerts on the right.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: A diagram showing the three-column layout with labels. Use different background colors or borders to distinguish each column. Include arrows or annotations explaining the purpose of each column. -->

<h2>Daily Task List</h2>

<p>
    The Daily Task List is your personal to-do list for the day. It's separate from renewal tasks and is designed for quick, ad-hoc items you need to remember.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>How to use it:</strong>
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Add tasks</strong> – Type a task and press Enter to add it to your list</li>
    <li><strong>Reorder tasks</strong> – Drag tasks up or down to prioritize them</li>
    <li><strong>Complete tasks</strong> – Check off tasks as you finish them</li>
    <li><strong>Remove tasks</strong> – Delete tasks you no longer need</li>
</ul>

<p>
    These tasks are just for you—they don't appear on renewals or in team reports. They're perfect for personal reminders like "Call John about the quote" or "Follow up on certificate request."
</p>

