<h2>Renewal Flow Tasks</h2>

<p>
    Renewal Flow Tasks show you the next steps for renewals you're working on. These are tasks that are part of actual renewals in the system, not personal reminders.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>What you'll see:</strong>
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Today's tasks</strong> – Tasks with goal dates of today that need attention</li>
    <li><strong>Upcoming tasks</strong> – Tasks coming up soon so you can plan ahead</li>
    <li><strong>Overdue tasks</strong> – Tasks that are past their goal date (highlighted so you notice them)</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>The "Show All" button:</strong>
</p>

<p>
    By default, Renewal Flow Tasks shows you a focused view of what's most important. Click the <strong>"Show All"</strong> button to see:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>All tasks for your renewals, not just today's items</li>
    <li>Tasks that are further out on the calendar</li>
    <li>A complete picture of all renewal work in progress</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Use "Show All" when you want to see the big picture or plan ahead. Use the focused view when you want to concentrate on what needs attention right now.
</p>

