<h2>Work Tiles (Middle Column)</h2>

<p>
    The middle column contains "work tiles"—widgets that show high-volume items that need quick action. These are designed so you can clear through work efficiently.
</p>

<h3>Proposal Pipeline</h3>

<p>
    Shows proposals that are in progress or need attention. Click on a proposal to open it and continue working.
</p>

<h3>Certificate Requests</h3>

<p>
    Lists certificate requests that need to be created or sent. Each item shows who requested it and when.
</p>

<h3>Leads</h3>

<p>
    Displays recent leads or leads that need follow-up. Quick access to your new business pipeline.
</p>

<p>
    Each tile shows items as cards or rows. You can typically click on an item to open it, or use action buttons to complete work directly from the homepage.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the middle column showing several work tiles. Highlight one tile (like Certificate Requests) showing multiple items listed. Show an example of clicking on an item or using an action button. Use callouts to identify each tile type. -->

<h2>Alerts and Reminders (Right Column)</h2>

<p>
    The right column highlights important items that need your attention but might not be urgent enough for the middle column.
</p>

<h3>Expiring Soon</h3>

<p>
    Shows policies that are expiring in the near future. This helps you stay ahead of renewals and avoid last-minute rushes.
</p>

<h3>Incomplete Tasks</h3>

<p>
    Lists tasks that are overdue or need a nudge. These are tasks from renewals or other work that haven't been completed yet.
</p>

<p>
    Check this column when you have a few minutes between calls or other work. It's a good place to find items that need attention but aren't necessarily urgent.
</p>

